{"timeLimit":5400,"questions":[{"question":"\\( 55 + 66 = ? \\)","options":["\\( 74 \\)","\\( 82 \\)","\\( 108 \\)","\\( 121 \\)","\\( 172 \\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 55 + 66 = 110 + 11 = 121 \\)."],"hint":"Add tens and ones separately: \\( 50+60=110 \\) and \\( 5+6=11 \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"\\( \\dfrac{36}{4} = ? \\)","options":["\\( 2 \\)","\\( 4 \\)","\\( 6 \\)","\\( 8 \\)","\\( 9 \\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 36 \\div 4 = 9 \\)."],"hint":"How many \\( 4 \\)s make \\( 36 \\)?","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"\\( 9 \\times 7 = ? \\)","options":["\\( 42 \\)","\\( 56 \\)","\\( 60 \\)","\\( 63 \\)","\\( 72 \\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 9 \\times 7 = 63 \\)."],"hint":"Use the nine-times table.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Calculate \\( 2040 - 40 + 40 - 2000 \\).","options":["\\( 10 \\)","\\( 4040 \\)","\\( 40 \\)","\\( 80 \\)","\\( 2040 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 2040 - 2000 = 40 \\), and \\( -40+40=0 \\), so the answer is \\( 40 \\)."],"hint":"\\( -40 + 40 \\) cancels out.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which number is NOT between \\( 5{,}345 \\) and \\( 7{,}216 \\)?","options":["\\( 5{,}499 \\)","\\( 7{,}539 \\)","\\( 6{,}499 \\)","\\( 5{,}985 \\)","\\( 7{,}198 \\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 7{,}539 > 7{,}216 \\), so it lies outside the range."],"hint":"A number is between them only if it is larger than \\( 5{,}345 \\) and smaller than \\( 7{,}216 \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"\\( 1 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 9 + 11 = ? \\)","options":["\\( 8 \\)","\\( 13 \\)","\\( 22 \\)","\\( 28 \\)","\\( 36 \\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["There are \\( 6 \\) odd numbers, so the sum is \\( 6^2 = 36 \\)."],"hint":"The sum of the first \\( n \\) odd numbers is \\( n^2 \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Today is a Saturday. After how many days will it be a Saturday again?","options":["\\( 42 \\)","\\( 36 \\)","\\( 30 \\)","\\( 25 \\)","\\( 18 \\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"explanation":["Only \\( 42 = 6 \\times 7 \\) is a multiple of \\( 7 \\)."],"hint":"Weekdays repeat every \\( 7 \\) days, so the answer must be a multiple of \\( 7 \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Aisha has \\( 6 \\) apples. How many apples will be left if she eats \\( \\dfrac{2}{3} \\) of the apples?","options":["\\( 0 \\)","\\( 1 \\)","\\( 2 \\)","\\( 3 \\)","\\( 5 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( \\frac{2}{3}\\times 6 = 4 \\) eaten, so \\( 6 - 4 = 2 \\) left (i.e. \\( \\frac{1}{3}\\times 6 \\))."],"hint":"She eats \\( \\frac{2}{3} \\) and keeps \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Saudatu wants to read a book of \\( 200 \\) pages. Every day she reads \\( 25 \\) pages. In how many days can she finish the book?","options":["\\( 4 \\)","\\( 6 \\)","\\( 8 \\)","\\( 10 \\)","\\( 12 \\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 200 \\div 25 = 8 \\) days."],"hint":"Divide total pages by pages per day.","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Evaluate \\( 1 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 6 \\).","options":["\\( 140 \\)","\\( 100 \\)","\\( 80 \\)","\\( 65 \\)","\\( 44 \\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"explanation":["\\( 2 + 12 + 30 = 44 \\)."],"hint":"Do the multiplications first (order of operations).","image":null,"topic":null,"type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Dalton has \\( 10 \\) cats as shown below. How many white cats should be sent away so that half of the remaining cats will be black?","options":["\\( 1 \\)","\\( 2 \\)","\\( 3 \\)","\\( 4 \\)","\\( 5